    {
      "heading": "Draining a tank",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A tank drains. Here is the volume over time.",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y10/maths/average-rate-of-change-tank.svg",
          "alt": "Tank volume falling from 200 L at 0 min to 140 L at 15 min with a chord from 0 to 10 minutes"
        },
        {
          "say": "From 0 to 10 minutes, it drops 50 litres.",
          "write": "(150 − 200) ÷ (10 − 0)"
        },
        {
          "say": "Fifty divided by ten. Minus 5 litres per minute.",
          "write": "−5 L/min"
        },
        {
          "say": "From 10 to 15 minutes, it is minus 2 litres per minute.",
          "write": "−10 ÷ 5 = −2 L/min"
        },
        {
          "say": "The draining is slowing down."
        },
        {
          "say": "Check. Minus five times ten is minus fifty. It works.",
          "write": "−5 × 10 = −50 ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "What the sign means",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Positive means it went up overall. Negative means it went down.",
          "write": "+ up,  − down"
        },
        {
          "say": "A ball’s height is twenty t take five t squared.",
          "write": "h = 20t − 5t²"
        },
        {
          "say": "First second: zero to fifteen metres. Fifteen metres per second.",
          "write": "15 m/s"
        },
        {
          "say": "From 1 to 3 seconds, it starts and ends at 15 metres.",
          "write": "(15 − 15) ÷ 2 = 0"
        },
        {
          "say": "So the average is zero. But the ball went up and came back down.",
          "write": "zero ≠ stopped"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "From average to instant",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Make the interval shorter and shorter, starting at x equals 2.",
          "write": "x = 2"
        },
        {
          "say": "Two to three gives 5. Two to 2.1 gives 4.1.",
          "write": "5,  4.1,  4.01 …"
        },
        {
          "say": "The answers close in on 4.",
          "write": "→ 4"
        },
        {
          "say": "The chord becomes the tangent. Its gradient is the instant rate.",
          "write": "instant = tangent",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y10/maths/average-rate-of-change-tangent.svg",
          "alt": "Chord from (2, 4) to (3, 9) and tangent at (2, 4)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Subtract in the same order, top and bottom. End minus start.",
          "write": "end − start"
        },
        {
          "say": "Always divide by the run. Change in y alone is not a rate."
        },
        {
          "say": "It is y over x. Do not flip it.",
          "write": "rise ÷ run"
        },
        {
          "say": "Two hours thirty minutes is 2.5 hours, not 2.3.",
          "write": "2 h 30 min = 2.5 h"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
